; Hand posed to wrap a grip. Its origin sits at the CENTRE of the grip
; it holds, so the arm rig can drop it straight onto a weapon's grip
; marker regardless of which weapon that is.
;
; Fingers are capsules rather than boxes: a finger is round, and these are held
; a hand's width from the camera in first person, which is the closest look
; anybody gets at any part of the soldier. The wrist ball at the origin fills
; the joint whichever way the forearm comes in, so the sleeve never separates
; from the hand mid-reload.
